          "source_text_sha256": "9922142a1f30575c977ccc94dd5122b6937d212bee18c2e8f44bdb408be05cca",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On June 30, 2015, the GEIPAN received a questionnaire regarding an observation made on November 10, 2012 at 9:30 PM by a single witness. The witness, on their terrace, observed in the sky a dark triangular phenomenon with angles and a center illuminated in a yellow-orange color. It moves at a low speed without noise, then rotates 90 degrees and heads full west at a blinding speed. Given the elements gathered in the investigation report (see attached document), namely:\n\n- Yellow-orange color identical to that of lanterns.\n- Behavior identical to that of objects subject to no or weak wind.\n- Short observation duration (less than 1 minute) compatible with the lifespan of lanterns.\n- Date: a Saturday night, compatible with those conducive to the organization of lantern releases for celebrations.\n- Number compatible with the amount of lanterns launched.\n- Illusion of acceleration and disappearance caused by the lanterns' extinction.\n- 90-degree turn possibly caused by a horizontal shear phenomenon.\n\nThe GEIPAN classifies this observation case as \"B,\" indicating a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "b1c50c04a1826c3cef3f2ece66a36e1128819bed646fce93df869c3f732f815f"
        }
      ],
